{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-hodge-star-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-hodge-star-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical Hodge star","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-hodge-star-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-hodge-star-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","hodge-star"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalHodgeStar.unique","text":"categorical-hodge-star-unique.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-hodge-star-unique\"></a><p>Given a fixed Frobenius form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\int_A</code> and volume form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{vol}</code>, the <a href=\"#def:categorical-hodge-star\">categorical Hodge star</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star</code> is uniquely determined. The defining Frobenius pairing pins it down. Any other involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star'</code> satisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha \\wedge \\star' \\beta = \\int_A(\\alpha^* \\cdot \\beta) \\mathrm{vol}</code> coincides with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\star</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-hodge-star-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"2.6.8"}
